1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:05,273
Five weeks ago in Durham, a roof came down on a firefighter searching a burning building.

2
00:00:05,353 --> 00:00:06,650
It keeps happening.

3
00:00:06,730 --> 00:00:12,233
In Houston, in 2013, the roof came down twelve minutes after the first engine arrived.

4
00:00:12,313 --> 00:00:14,636
Four firefighters never came out.

5
00:00:14,766 --> 00:00:19,949
The state fire marshal's first finding was simple. There were no pre-fire plans for that building.

6
00:00:20,029 --> 00:00:23,437
No site diagram. No record of how it was built.

7
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:28,506
Plans like that come from an officer walking the building with a clipboard.

8
00:00:28,586 --> 00:00:30,622
Nobody can walk every building.

9
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:36,935
Last year a Georgia firefighter died in a warehouse where, NIOSH wrote, no pre-incident plan was available.

10
00:00:37,015 --> 00:00:39,108
The old ones sat in binders.

11
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:45,279
The facts are already out there, in data nobody hands to the fire service.

12
00:00:45,359 --> 00:00:47,434
Here's a warehouse in east LA.

13
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:50,398
Our agent sends three analysts out at once.

14
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,131
CoStar knows what's inside.

15
00:00:53,211 --> 00:00:58,824
A 1969 concrete tilt-up, a health-and-beauty wholesaler, eleven dock doors.

16
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:04,002
The Matterport scan shows a steel mezzanine stair and pallets stacked on the floor.

17
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:11,511
Vexcel shows solar across the roof, the walls a ladder truck can actually reach, and where to park it.

18
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:17,949
Every line cites a source. Hydrants it can't see, so it says verify on site, never a guess.

19
00:01:18,029 --> 00:01:20,799
Nothing goes to a crew until an officer signs off.

20
00:01:20,879 --> 00:01:22,462
Even from a text.

21
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:40,523
Fire departments already pay for pre-planning software, and FEMA prevention grants fund it.

22
00:01:40,603 --> 00:01:45,293
A city's insurance grade rewards pre-planning every commercial building, every year.

23
00:01:45,373 --> 00:01:48,241
With our draft waiting, the walk becomes a check.

24
00:01:48,321 --> 00:01:52,353
We sell per building, inside the software departments already use.

25
00:01:52,433 --> 00:01:56,097
We've already indexed 3,288 buildings in Houston and LA.

26
00:01:56,177 --> 00:01:59,318
The next crew should know the building before they're inside it.

